# Project Blueprint

Before answering questions about architecture, routing, permissions, or feature scope, read the relevant blueprint Markdown (not DOCX).

## Module → file

| Module | File |
|--------|------|
| Admin | `docs/admin.md` |

When the module is unclear, ask which module applies. Do **not** load every blueprint by default.

## Stack notes

- Frontend: React (this repo). Prefer existing project patterns over blueprint mentions of Tailwind/Zustand/React Query if the codebase already uses Mantine/Redux Toolkit, etc.
- Backend APIs: implement in **NestJS** (`sunbird-core-backend-nestjs`), not Java/Spring — even when the blueprint names Spring Boot, JPA, or `@PreAuthorize`.

## Working style

- Prefer `@docs/<module>.md` plus a section reference (e.g. §7.1) in the user prompt.
- Product behavior in the blueprint wins; framework snippets in the blueprint do not.
